WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.480
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.650
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.200
The S4 Selection finally starts next week.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.570
That gets me going!

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.370
We'll be putting our past year of Aikatsu to the test.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.410
Yep!

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.580
By the way,

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.830
there's still the matter of my dress for the Selection.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:29.420
I was hoping to acquire special Grade-up Glitter and create a dress unique to me.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.420
Yeah, I'll be rooting for you!{I consider this the default translation but I don't think we've used it once}{but then she literally... oh right, you don't watch the episode}

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.630
How did you acquire your Glitter?

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:35.720
I guess...

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.220
Congratulations!

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.100
Yuri-senpai.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.230
I'll show you how to get your hands on some special Grade-up Glitter! {or if you want to be boring 'let me teach you'}{there's not-boring and then there's silly}{how dare you insult ye olde English}

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.480
And how would that be?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.480
Basically, all you've got to do is pull off a huge show!

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.490
A huge show?

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:58.490
Come to think of it, I got mine after I performed on that music show.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.410
Yeah, and we got it after our unit performance.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:03.500
Right.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.330
A simple matter, then.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.210
I, Saotome Ako, will dazzle you with a fabulous performance!

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:50.100
The first thing you've gotta do is reserve yourself a venue.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.190
Good point.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.690
Rola and Mahiru-chan, you guys got a slot for the school's mini-theater, right?

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.110
Yeah. The schedule was full,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.700
but we got them to squeeze us in somehow.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.290
Yeah, and there was no guarantee it wouldn't be canceled.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.500
But we had to take a chance and try. {I liked this}

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.420
Okay, I'll go and petition Momoko-sensei right away.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.380
Pardon me, Momoko-sensei!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.140
How'd it go, Ako-chan?

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.640
Complete failure.{wow, by slightly changing the formation the words took on different syntax}

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:30.270
If the academy's full up, 
you should try looking outside.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:32.940
Let's go!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.560
Wait!

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.950
Yume, do you have any leads?

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.660
Check it!{have you seen/read/played/listened to sister princess? if so, rank them please}{unfortunately, no}

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.540
What is that supposed to be?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.040
A list of places Katsura-senpai and the admins gave me before.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.340
Let's go through them together.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:07.260
I-If you insist that much on seeing my performance, I suppose I wouldn't mind accompanying you.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.600
Come along! Let's get started, Yume!

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.950
I've never met a flight attendant like you before.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.950
You're only getting in my way. Go home!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.330
No, I will not go anywhere!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.250
It's as though I'm looking at a younger me.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:39.090
No matter what happens, I will see my dream through to the end!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.090
What a touching film.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.800
Tsubasacchi, that was your best work yet!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:48.600
I agree.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.100
I'm glad you liked it.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.060
The kitten was clumsy and slow!

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.610
I love the kitten!

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.820
Sounds like it got the kids demographic too.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:05.990
Honestly, it wouldn't have been such a hit if not for Saotome's influence.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.990
Ako-chan's?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:13.160
Because Saotome put her soul into the role, the resulting work was given depth.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.370
She's grown more than I anticipated.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.500
It's not only Ako-chan.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:23.550
Yume-chan is making her way to me one step at a time.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:34.980
Mahiru is making a name for herself as a different type of model from me.{arbitrary mezashite house rule based on antiquated style guides and a misguided adherence to an imagined literary tradition #17: "different than" is not a thing}{I will still never remember which we do, so yoroshiku}

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:40.310
All of them are making efforts to surpass us.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.360
I don't want to lose.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:50.410
At some point, it became more appropriate to call them rivals than schoolmates.{this is the first time since chiisa na tenohira that I've seen "itsu kara ka", which is weird because I feel like that shouldn't be the case}{seriously?}

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.120
Rivals. Yes, they certainly are.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:59.500
It seems we won't be able to spend the rest of our half-day off sitting on our butts.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:03.750
All right! Let's go and train!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.340
Yeah!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.850
That's another place we can cross off the list.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.980
But there must be space somewhere.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.730
Okay, next up...

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.440
Why are you going this far?

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.530
Because you're my precious friend.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:28.490
Yume...

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.160
I'll work something out on my own.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:36.040
You return to the academy and focus on your own Aikatsu.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.040
But...

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.460
Need I repeat myself?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:43.420
I would feel awful if you didn't make it into S4 because you were helping me!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:48.420
Got it. Ako-chan, hang in there!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.430
Don't worry, I have no intention of giving up!

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.650
No luck here, either.{das ist nicht was es bedeutet}{don't even, it definitely is}

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.290
It's the kitten!

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.670
The clumsy and slow kitten!

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:25.710
My, you saw the movie I was in? 
Thank you very much.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.420
Hey, hey! I wanna hear that line!

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.590
The one from the movie!

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.590
I would be glad to.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:38.310
No matter what happens, I will see my dream through to the end!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.350
Awesome!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:51.610
Attention kids! The Superhero Battlemen stage show is about to start!

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:54.370
Everyone gather round!

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.450
A stage!

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:02.370
The Superhero Battlemen came all this way to see you! {battlemen?}{also vielleicht battlemans, und soll es nicht "Superhero" sein?}{yeah, I don't know what I was thinking}

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:05.790
You can shake our hands at the Kira Kira Department Store!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.130
There was a stage here all along!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:17.180
Excuse me, would it be possible for me to reserve some time at the stage here?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:23.020
We would be honored to host a show for an idol of Four Star Academy...

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.650
What to do...

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.940
Is there any way we can make it work?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.070
I wanna see the kitten on stage!

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.530
I wanna see too!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:35.110
Understood. I'll rearrange this and fit you in.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.370
You will?

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.870
Yes. Let's take a look.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:40.910
How does Saturday at noon sound?

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.790
That would be perfect!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.420
Yay!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.040
This is all thanks to you.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:49.040
I'll put on a show you'll never forget!

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.250
You said it!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.800
It's a promise!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.510
I promise.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.840
Promise!

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:04.310
Aikatsu! Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.310
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.810
Aikatsu! Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.100
Hime-senpai.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.070
Yume-chan, follow us!

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.330
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!{vermutlich war das keine absicht}

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.090
Wow, none of you in S4 are out of breath at all.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.720
You'll have to work harder to pass us.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:37.930
Right!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:44.890
With that said, I hope you will be able to come and see my show.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.440
Best wishes.{das erinnert mir an crime edge}{I love her too}

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.820
He should be arriving soon.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.500
Subaru-kyun, welcome home!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.500
Uh...

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:09.880
I'm back.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.340
Why are you here?

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.590
Where is my Subaru-kyun?!

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:20.890
Him? They added him into new scenes, so he's out filming on location.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.760
Then what about my concert on Saturday?

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.930
I just so happen to be off that day.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.560
And I would rather you spend it anywhere else!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.280
You wished to see me, Tsubasa-senpai?

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:45.540
Yeah, sorry to call you here so late.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.500
It's fine. What did you want to discuss?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:53.040
I'd like you to make a guest appearance at my next show.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.170
A guest appearance? You want me?

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:01.550
There will be several others from 
Theater Class, but I wanted to invite you too.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.050
Momoko-sensei has already approved it.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:08.560
I will gladly join you! When will it be?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.690
It starts at noon on Saturday.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.770
Saturday at noon?

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.860
You said it!

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.690
It's a promise!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.240
Promise!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.200
Did you have plans?

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.120
No...

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.090
What now? What now? What now?

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:44.090
What now? What now? What now? What now?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:49.100
It's an honor to be personally invited to join Tsubasa-senpai on stage.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:52.230
But I already made a promise with the kids...

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:54.690
I've got it!

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:59.610
In times like these, I simply need to do a full scan of my mental database to find the answer.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:08.990
Tick tick tick tick...

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.950
Saotome-san?

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.500
Does not compute!

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.000
What am I supposed to do?!

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.630
I see, so that's what's troubling you.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.510
My promise with the children came first.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:24.510
I know full well that I should be prioritizing them...

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:29.770
But it's hard to pass up an opportunity to be with Tsubasa-senpai, considering she's in S4.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.810
Yes...

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:35.810
Saotome-san, I don't want you to have any regrets, so listen carefully.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:37.020
Okay.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:45.160
Like I said before, you need to pull off a huge show in order to get the special Grade-up Glitter.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.320
I remember.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.910
The condition for that is to satisfy a large audience.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.410
A large audience...

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.460
Tsubasa-senpai's show will be in the academy's private grand hall.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.880
Compared to the roof of Kira Kira Department Store...

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:09.390
No matter how spectacular the show, it would be impossible to get a Grade-up Glitter.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.970
Honestly, it's a tough decision.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:16.940
But both of them are important, so be sure to think it through.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:17.860
Okay.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:23.740
Really? You got a special Grade-up Glitter?

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.530
Now I'll be able to make a unique dress!

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.950
What about me?

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.330
<i>The S4 Selection is almost here.</i>

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:38.080
<i>This dress is far from being only my own.</i>

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.380
<i>Were I to use it...</i>

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.670
Ako-chan!

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:47.720
You did it, Ako-chan!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:48.510
What?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:51.310
We heard you're going to be in Tsubasa-senpai's show!

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.310
Something wrong?

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:58.810
I've made my decision.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.480
We're only one week away from the S4 Selection.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:08.950
My next performance will be my last chance to get myself Grade-up Glitter.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.990
I have to go with Tsubasa-senpai!

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.620
<i>It pains my heart to break our promise.</i>

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.880
<i>But I'm sure they'll understand if I explain myself.</i>

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.130
<i>Because those children...</i>

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.130
<i>Are my fans!</i>

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.390
It's the kitten!

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:33.310
Isn't it great?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.890
Do you like it?

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:36.890
Why...

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:41.610
The empty stage seemed lonely, so they decided to decorate it.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.980
It seems they're infatuated with you.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.780
'Cause we're your fans!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.030
And not normal fans!

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.030
We're huge fans!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.660
My fans...

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.910
That's right.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.580
Subaru-kyun!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:03.130
<i>I, as a fan of Subaru-kyun myself,</i>

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.340
<i>should have known how my own fans felt better than anyone.</i>

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.300
Thank you.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:13.850
<i>But...</i>

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.190
I'm sorry.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.940
It's time to introduce my guests!

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.990
First up is Sakamoto Arisa!

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:37.080
Next we have Hasumi Shouko.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.960
And finally...

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.960
I'm Saotome Ako!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.960
Everyone, good afternoon! {how do you do these again?}

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.460
Good afternoon!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:54.970
Today, Saotome Ako-chan from Four Star Academy has come to sing for you!

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:59.220
<i>Tsubasa-senpai, I'm sorry.</i>

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.390
We made it.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:05.110
Ako must have been distraught over which show to do.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.150
I didn't realize at all.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:10.990
If we'd noticed, we would've helped her however we could.

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:17.490
Everyone! I'm here for all of you, for all of my precious fans.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:20.000
I'll sing with all my heart!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.460
Saotome Ako, making a dazzling entrance!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.790
Ako-chan, that was a great performance!

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.750
All the children were cheering hard.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:55.420
Thanks. Though as I expected,

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:59.050
I didn't get a special Grade-up Glitter.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.050
Ako-chan, you're the best!

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.800
Hey, hey! I wanna hear that line again!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.430
Sure, of course.

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:12.440
No matter what happens, I will see my dream through to the end!

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:14.440
One more time please!

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:19.690
No matter what happens, I will see my dream through to the end!

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.950
Again! Again!

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.820
No matter what happens...

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.450
I will see my dream through to the end!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:36.590
Tsubasa-senpai, I sincerely apologize for today!

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:37.960
Don't worry about it.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:42.630
It was my fault for inviting you without first asking about your plans.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.470
No, not at all!

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:48.850
Let's fight fair and square during next week's S4 Selection.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:51.220
Yes!

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:54.770
Ako-chan, are you in?

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.770
I'm coming in...

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:00.860
Ako-chan?

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.820
Nijino Yume...

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:06.740
Did I make the right choice?

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.580
Huh? What do you mean?

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:14.370
Had I chosen to attend Tsubasa-senpai's show,
 I could have gotten Grade-up Glitter.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:17.290
I think I would've done the same thing you did.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.750
You would have?

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:24.260
Yeah. There are things more important than some Grade-up Glitter.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:29.510
You didn't make a mistake.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.010
Yume.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:37.440
But of course! I had already known that from the start.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.910
On The Radio Music.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:49.070
Tonight brought to you by Kira Kanata...

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:51.660
And Yuuki Subaru.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.410
Subaru-kyun!

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.120
Okay, time to train.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:59.540
I want to kick us off tonight by talking about a certain idol.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:02.300
Huh, that's rare coming from you.

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:06.800
She turned down a big opportunity to make headway toward her dream,

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:09.050
instead opting to perform for her fans.

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:11.180
Wow, that's awesome.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:13.850
Yeah, and it was a fantastic performance.

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:18.810
Besides, anyone who would betray their fans has no right to call themselves an idol.

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:21.230
She passes in my book.

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.340
The S4 Selection has begun.

